Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Copper Wires Unraveling
- Story & Context: In the Sector-9 intersection, Jace realizes the city grid has stopped reporting heartbeat data, so he plugs his deck into the local signal box as the first car honks in the rain. "The static is the only truth I keep," he murmurs while the lights begin to stutter in perfect time with his kick drum. The transition from silence to controlled chaos marks the birth of the protest, grounding the city in a new, dangerous rhythm.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up shot of raw copper wires being pulled apart with pliers, glowing with inner heat, dark moody industrial background, abstract artistic representation of electricity flowing into concrete.

Track 2: What Color Do You Need?
- Story & Context: Kael sits inside the locked control tower of Central Junction, counting the seconds until the next light-cycle while watching the crowd grow impatient and loud. She whispers her confession into the broadcast channel, asking the grid if the people truly want safety or just a distraction from the encroaching darkness. "If I turn it green, will you finally let me leave?" she sings, her voice cracking against the mechanical pulse of the city.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A blurry silhouette of a person inside a glowing glass observation booth surrounded by thousands of red traffic light reflections, poetic and lonely vibe.

Track 3: The Weaver Mends The Curb
- Story & Context: Years after the blackout, the intersection has become a holy site where people leave scraps of fabric and discarded microchips to honor the night the lights sang. Mara stands at the center of the ring, stitching a line of conductive silver thread into her palm as the rhythmic thumping of the underground bass vibrates the pavement. She chants the memory of the first night, knowing that "the pattern holds even when the world forgets," and the community begins to dance until the sun comes up to challenge the fading streetlights.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A grand, wide shot of a crowd in a concrete intersection illuminated by thousands of small, hand-woven lanterns, ethereal and ritualistic atmosphere, intricate weaving patterns superimposed over the night sky.

